   "source": [
    "I don’t have the CI logs or job file yet. Please attach the failing job logs (the pytest traceback) and the CI job definition (e.g., .github/workflows/*, .gitlab-ci.yml, or the job log snippet) so I can pinpoint the failure. Meanwhile, you can reproduce the failure locally and capture a focused log with these commands:\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b9f28f5e",
   "metadata": {
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "bash"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "# run entire file (verbose)\n",
    "pytest -q -vv /home/ahi5/_workspace_/danny663788/Marlin/Marlin-sample-01/baseline/openai-python-4e28a4/tests/api_resources/chat/test_completions.py -s --maxfail=1\n",
    "\n",
    "# or run a single failing test (replace TEST_NAME with the test function name)\n",
    "pytest -q -vv -k TEST_NAME /home/ahi5/_workspace_/danny663788/Marlin/Marlin-sample-01/baseline/openai-python-4e28a4/tests/api_resources/chat/test_completions.py -s --maxfail=1\n",
    "\n",
    "# include environment variable used by tests if needed\n",
    "TEST_API_BASE_URL=\"http://127.0.0.1:4010\" pytest -q -vv ...same path... -s"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "73fa4291",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Share:\n",
    "- the pytest traceback output (full stack trace)\n",
    "- the CI job YAML or job logs that show environment variables and installed deps\n",
    "- which test(s) failed (name(s))\n",
    "\n",
    "With that I will propose the exact code/test/CI fix."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9a3e9c33",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Add the missing imports at the top of the test file. The type errors come from undefined names like os, json, pytest, httpx, and pydantic.\n",
    "\n",
    "Apply this change:\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f0580f17",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# ...existing code...\n",
    "from respx import MockRouter\n",
    "\n",
    "import os\n",
    "import json\n",
    "import pytest\n",
    "import httpx\n",
    "import pydantic\n",
    "# ...existing code..."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "63ae1209",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "./scripts/lint``"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "35f4065c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Use a typed intermediate value before `json.loads`.  \n",
    "`respx` call objects are coming through as unknown to Pyright in strict mode, so chained access (`route.calls[0].request.content.decode()`) triggers `reportUnknownMemberType`.\n",
    "\n",
    "Apply this change:\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "bcdfbddc",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# ...existing code...\n",
    "        assert route.called\n",
    "        call = cast(Any, route.calls[0])\n",
    "        request_content = cast(bytes, call.request.content)\n",
    "        request_body = json.loads(request_content.decode(\"utf-8\"))\n",
    "        assert request_body[\"web_search_options\"][\"include_domains\"] == [\"github.com\", \"*.gov\"]\n",
    "        assert request_body[\"web_search_options\"][\"exclude_domains\"] == [\"example.com\", \"*.edu\"]\n",
    "# ...existing code..."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e666dfc3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Then run:\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0df93a91",
   "metadata": {
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "bash"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "./scripts/format\n",
    "./scripts/lint"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f2078622",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "This keeps lint formatting intact and removes the Pyright unknown-member errors on line 81."
   ]
