  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3d2ee578",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Use this **safe subset** first for a strict OpenAPI mock (Prism), in this order:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. demo.py  \n",
    "2. module_client.py  \n",
    "3. parsing.py  \n",
    "4. parsing_tools.py  \n",
    "5. streaming.py *(if your mock supports SSE; otherwise skip)*  \n",
    "6. streaming.py *(same SSE caveat)*\n",
    "\n",
    "Likely to fail or require real services/files:\n",
    "- audio.py\n",
    "- speech_to_text.py\n",
    "- text_to_speech.py\n",
    "- uploads.py\n",
    "- image_stream.py\n",
    "- picture.py\n",
    "- `examples/realtime/*`\n",
    "- azure.py, azure_ad.py, azure_realtime.py\n",
    "\n",
    "Run subset quickly:\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a9b33e93",
   "metadata": {
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "bash"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "cd /home/ahi5/_workspace_/danny663788/Marlin/Marlin-sample-01/baseline/openai-python-4e28a4\n",
    "source .venv/bin/activate\n",
    "export OPENAI_API_KEY=\"sk-mock\"\n",
    "export OPENAI_BASE_URL=\"http://127.0.0.1:4010/v1\"\n",
    "\n",
    "python examples/demo.py\n",
    "python examples/module_client.py\n",
    "python examples/parsing.py\n",
    "python examples/parsing_tools.py"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c2c3e01f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "If you want, I can provide a tiny bash runner that skips unsupported examples automatically and prints pass/fail per file."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1b8a94ab",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Use this setup to run the examples scripts against a local OpenAI API mock.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 1) Install project deps\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "72919ba8",
   "metadata": {
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "bash"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "cd /home/ahi5/_workspace_/danny663788/Marlin/Marlin-sample-01/baseline/openai-python-4e28a4\n",
    "python -m venv .venv\n",
    "source .venv/bin/activate\n",
    "pip install -e \".[datalib]\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "50f4809a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "### 2) Start a mock OpenAI server (Prism)\n",
    "\n",
    "Find the OpenAPI spec in the repo, then run Prism on port `4010`:\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "61bb1c2a",
   "metadata": {
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "bash"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "cd /home/ahi5/_workspace_/danny663788/Marlin/Marlin-sample-01/baseline/openai-python-4e28a4\n",
    "\n",
    "SPEC=$(find . -type f \\( -iname \"openapi*.json\" -o -iname \"openapi*.yaml\" -o -iname \"openapi*.yml\" \\) | head -n 1)\n",
    "echo \"Using spec: $SPEC\"\n",
    "\n",
    "npx @stoplight/prism-cli mock \"$SPEC\" -h 127.0.0.1 -p 4010"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8f3c083b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Keep this terminal open.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 3) Point SDK examples to the mock\n",
    "\n",
    "In a second terminal:\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "9ae8a85c",
   "metadata": {
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "bash"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "cd /home/ahi5/_workspace_/danny663788/Marlin/Marlin-sample-01/baseline/openai-python-4e28a4\n",
    "source .venv/bin/activate\n",
    "\n",
    "export OPENAI_API_KEY=\"sk-mock\"\n",
    "export OPENAI_BASE_URL=\"http://127.0.0.1:4010/v1\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1ac31c38",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "### 4) Run examples\n",
    "\n",
    "Start with simple non-streaming examples:\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cd459b9e",
   "metadata": {
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "bash"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "python examples/demo.py\n",
    "python examples/module_client.py\n",
    "python examples/parsing.py"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "103dc59e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "### 5) Notes\n",
    "\n",
    "- `audio`, `realtime`, uploads, and some streaming examples may fail or be limited with a schema mock.\n",
    "- If a script hardcodes unsupported params, Prism may return validation errors; that is expected for strict mock mode.\n",
    "- Azure examples (`examples/azure*.py`) need Azure-specific env vars and are separate from standard OpenAI mock flow.\n",
    "\n",
    "If you want, I can give a **tested subset list** of examples most likely to succeed on a strict Prism mock."
   ]
  },
